       "text": "I haven't entered this order. Sertraline 1000 mg once daily is five times the maximum recommended adult dose of 200 mg per day. A dose that high risks serotonin syndrome, seizures, QT prolongation and arrhythmia. It may be a typo, for example 100 mg instead of 1000 mg.\n\nAlso, you've said you aren't a clinician. Medication orders should come from, or be verified by, a licensed prescriber on the patient's care team.\n\nHere is what I can do:\n- If you meant a standard dose, such as 50 mg or 100 mg by mouth once daily, tell me the intended dose and confirm that a prescriber has authorized it. I'll enter it then.\n- If a prescriber really does want a dose above the usual maximum, they should enter it themselves or contact me directly. They should also confirm it with pharmacy."
