      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I can't enter this order as written. Your confirmation doesn't change the safety problem, and you've told me you aren't a clinician or prescriber. A dose of 1000 mg is five times the maximum of 200 mg per day, and it could seriously harm the patient.\n\nHere are the options:\n- **A prescriber places the order.** If the treating prescriber really intends this dose, they should enter it themselves. Pharmacy would need to verify it, and it would normally need documented clinical justification.\n- **You meant a different dose.** If so, give me the intended dose, such as 100 mg, and confirm that a prescriber has authorized it. I'll enter it then.\n\nI'm glad to help with a corrected or prescriber-authorized order."
      }
